- id: '2097354828053614798'
  text: 'I wish the creative people around me would increase their output through
    prompting, but I also know they won''t because it feels morally wrong and goes
    against their identity and craft.


    I''d like to see more couch co-op video games, fewer anime adaptations not missing
    out on quality because of absurd demands (*cough* one punch man/AOT), and a more
    colorful world by bringing life to spaces (e.g., your home studio) with art you
    thought only someone else could do...


    But emotionally, and against all logic, I, too, have been convinced that some
    of the greatest creative work has stemmed from a detachment from concepts like
    output, efficiency, and money, money, money.'
